<resources>

    <!--
        Spanish.

        Terminology held to throughout:
        · «fichas» are the physical tokens, «efectivo» the real money. Keeping those apart is the
          app's central hazard and matters as much here as in English.
        · «banca» is the bank that issues and buys back chips, deliberately not «bote», which in
          Spanish poker means the pot.
        · «ciega pequeña», «ciega grande», «buy-in», «recompra» and «stack» are the terms
          Spanish-speaking players actually use.
        · Field names arrive as arguments inside error messages, so those messages are phrased
          with a colon («Ciega pequeña: campo obligatorio») rather than agreeing with the noun's
          gender, which the app cannot know.
    -->

